Quake II's mode table has no 16:9 entry, so on a 1280x720 or 1920x1080
display the closest gl_mode (5: 960x720) runs in a window smaller than the
screen, which X can only composite by a copy, never page flip. Fullscreen
already switches to the closest X mode at least as large; with a matching
table entry the window covers the screen.

  ...setting mode 5: 960 720

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

--- a/src/vid_so.c	2026-11-23 13:01:34.636698143 +0100
+++ b/src/vid_so.c	2026-11-23 13:01:58.088227049 +0100
@@ -167,7 +167,9 @@ vidmode_t vid_modes[] = {
     { "Mode 11: 1024x480",  1024,  480, 11 }, /* Sony VAIO Pocketbook */
     { "Mode 12: 1152x768",  1152,  768, 12 }, /* Apple TiBook */
     { "Mode 13: 1280x854",  1280,  854, 13 }, /* Apple TiBook */
-    { "Mode 14: 1440x900",  1440,  900, 14 }  /* Apple 17" Powerbook G4 */
+    { "Mode 14: 1440x900",  1440,  900, 14 }, /* Apple 17" Powerbook G4 */
+    { "Mode 15: 1280x720",  1280,  720, 15 },
+    { "Mode 16: 1920x1080", 1920, 1080, 16 }
 };
 
 qboolean VID_GetModeInfo( unsigned int *width, unsigned int *height, int mode )
